{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/869530-origins-game-fair-2016-last-minute-mtaw-2nd-game","id":869530,"title":"Origins Game Fair 2016 - last minute MtAw 2nd game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-20T12:27:07-07:00","id":869530,"title":"Origins Game Fair 2016 - last minute MtAw 2nd game?","content":"So, I feel like the official RPG events at Origins Game Fair this June in Columbus are pretty slim pickings for anyone who is not all about D&amp;D, Pathfinder, and Shadowrun... by the time the site would load for me once registration opened, any of the sparse events I would have scheduled were sold out, and I feel like I'll be at Indie Games on Demand one too many times already. My partner, however, was able to load up on events on certain days so I'll have long stretches with nothing to do but wander.<br /> <br /> So I'm thinking about trying to coordinate something with any other people who will also be there - find an empty table somewhere in the convention center and play or run Mage the Awakening 2nd edition (or Mindjammer RPG, but that's probably not of as much interest to people here at the OP forums.) I doubt the Advance PDF will take more than another week so that's plenty of time to prepare. I'm assuming I'm still going to almost completely focused on MtAw 2nd by mid-June.<br /> <br /> At first I thought, &quot;maybe I'll just carry some stuff with me and send out a tweet if I get bored.&quot; But the more I think about it, the more sending an invite to everyone following a hashtag sounds like a recipe for a chaotic mess. So I thought I'd gauge interest here.<br /> <br /> I need to fill time on Thursday the 16th from around 6-7pm until at least 10 or 11.<br /> <br /> Then I've got another gap on Friday the 17th from 8am until about 1pm. And we'd both possibly be open for something that same day after 6pm.<br /> <br /> Then again on Saturday the 18th from around 6-7pm until at least 10 or 11.<br /> <br /> Anyone else going to Origins and at a loss for how they'll fill their schedules around those times? Unfortunately, I don't think the car will make it to GenCon this year, and I was already registered for Origins before I saw how few events there would actually be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10592,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","user":"Phlox","date":". 04-20-2016, 03:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","name":"Phlox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T20:56:36-07:00","id":876239,"title":"","content":"For me, most of my convention days for Origins are filled with running/playing Star wars with the Sparks force 7 group...The only real 2 slots of the con i have open, are on thurs morning and Fri morning and ONLY if the slots i am in do not run/go off for what ever reason....<br /> BUT if nothing else, it would be nice to meet you.. That is if you are a C/bus local..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T16:59:00-07:00","id":878241,"title":"","content":"I am not, sadly. I live about three hours away in Pittsburgh. We like Columbus and it would be great to move there, we've talked about it and I'm originally from Ohio, but timing and finances are an issue. I may be running a regular game on Roll 20, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10592-phlox","name":"Phlox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}